data 379
Fix wide landscape player layout

Align wide-screen player chrome across the left/right panes by centralizing gutter math and cover sizing, moving the seek bar and transport cluster into the left pane when space allows, and falling back cleanly on narrower layouts. This also adds regression coverage for landscape symmetry, Zen-mode spacing, and small-screen fallback behavior.
from :1973
commit refs/heads/rust-local-force
mark :1975
author Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791146077 +0800
committer Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791146077 +0800
data 369
Add shared player cover shadow

Adds a reusable PlayerCoverShadow wrapper for full-player cover art and applies it to both MD3 and AM layouts. The shadow uses the cover radius, scales with cover size, and follows the theme shadow token instead of a hardcoded color. Includes regression tests covering radius consistency, size-based clamping, and shadow color behavior.
from :1974
commit refs/heads/rust-local-force
mark :1976
author Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791172859 +0800
committer Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791172859 +0800
data 622
Add cover shadow setting and capsule fixes

Added a persistent cover shadow intensity setting and synced it across both full-player cover wrappers via a shared notifier. The cover stack now keeps its shadow visible by disabling clipping at the outer wrapper, and the setting is exposed in the playback style settings with search indexing updates.

Also fixed the top-bar trailing capsule logic so the quality badge is treated independently from the generic collapse toggle, while preserving the existing expand/More behavior for other segments. Updated and added tests for the new shadow intensity and capsule edge cases.
from :1975
commit refs/heads/rust-local-force
mark :1977
author Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791178309 +0800
committer Koshca <155223948+Saul-Soul@users.noreply.github.com> 1791178309 +0800
data 447
Fix top-bar pill tap/animation states

Adjust the full-player top-bar trailing capsule so the more icon sits outside the pill background with the correct icon tint, and allow taps to execute as soon as the label starts revealing instead of waiting for the animation to finish. Added segment entry/exit animation keyed by semanticsLabel to keep expanded state stable when items appear/disappear, and updated widget tests to cover the new behavior.
